# The Linux socket options and socket ioctl requests that no vetted crate (rustix, socket2, nix, std) wraps safely.
# interface.rs and implementation/direct/generated.rs are made from this table by implementation/direct/tests/generated.rs, which
# fails when either differs from what the table gives; run it with REGENERATE=1 to write them.
#
# Columns: the method; the level (`-` for an ioctl request); the option or request; its value; the manual page that
# defines it; what the kernel does with the caller's memory. A method named set_* writes the option, get_* reads it.
#
# Kernel (from the manual page and the kernel's handler, and checked on the running kernel for every row by the
# direct implementation's probe, which surrounds the value with canary bytes and compares them after each call):
#   reads         a set: the kernel only reads the value, so the method takes it by shared reference or by copy
#   writes-back   a set: the kernel may write into the value, so the method takes it by exclusive reference
#   within        a get: the kernel writes at most the length it is told, often less, and never before the value
#   past          a get: the kernel may write past the length it is told (one answer per key asked)
#   through       a get: the kernel also writes at the addresses the value holds, within the counts and sizes it names
#
# Values:
#   bool          an int the kernel reads as off (0) or on (1)
#   c_int u32 u64 a number of that width
#   bytes         a byte string the kernel reads whole (set only)
#   room          a read of a value of varying length into a room whose size the caller names as a constant
#   struct:T      one value of the uapi type T (set only), by the reference the kernel column asks
#   slice:T       a run of values of the uapi type T (set only)
#   keys          one TCP_AO_GET_KEYS query, read back in place
#   program       a classic BPF program the kernel copies through `struct sock_fprog`
#   group_filter  a source filter the kernel reads as `struct group_filter`
#   full_info     an MPTCP_FULL_INFO read, the kernel writing the subflow arrays named in the value
#   ioctl         an ioctl request that writes one int
#
# method                           level            option                            value                          manual      kernel
set_so_rcvmark                     uapi::SOL_SOCKET uapi::SO_RCVMARK                  bool                           socket(7)   reads
set_so_rcvpriority                 uapi::SOL_SOCKET uapi::SO_RCVPRIORITY              bool                           socket(7)   reads
